\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Degrees of a cyclic action}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{\ell\ge1}, and let #{k} be a field containing a primitive
#{\ell}th root of unity #{\zeta}, with #{\ell} invertible in #{k}.
For a linear map #{g:V\to V} satisfying #{g^\ell=\bbI_V}, set
##{V_\nu=\ker(g-\zeta^\nu\bbI_V)
  \qquad(\nu\in\mathbb Z/\ell\mathbb Z).}
The decomposition into these spaces is the \newvocab{cyclic grading}
of #{g} for the chosen root. A vector in #{V_\nu} has degree #{\nu}.
A space #{V_\nu} may be zero. Only #{g^\ell=\bbI_V} is required.
An element of a \vocabk{stabilizer}{fdip-0164} acting on a
translation block supplies such a map whenever its order divides
#{\ell}.}
